# Tailwind / DRY frontend rule

When adding or changing marketing UI in this repo:

- **Tailwind in components.** Style with Tailwind utility classes in TSX
  (`className`), including `before:` / `after:` / `group-open:` / responsive
  variants. Do **not** add new component-specific rules to
  `src/app/globals.css`.
- **`globals.css` exceptions only:** `:root` design tokens, base reset, font
  utility bridges (`.font-serif-display`, `.font-mono-text` until moved into
  the Tailwind theme), and keyframes that cannot be expressed cleanly as
  utilities. No new `.faq-*`, `.comparison-*`, `.pack-*`, `.waitlist-*`,
  `.coming-soon-*`, etc. blocks.
- **Shared behavior → hooks** under `src/hooks/` (or `src/lib/gsap/` for GSAP
  helpers). Repeated GSAP section reveals use `useSectionReveal`. Subscribe
  forms use `useSubscribeForm`.
- **Shared chrome → UI primitives** under `src/components/ui/`. Prefer
  `SectionHeader`, `GoldButton` / `GhostButton`, and shared form components
  over copy-pasted eyebrow/headline/form markup.
- **One composition pattern per concern.** Do not invent a second subscribe
  form, section header, or reveal orchestration style.
- Migrating legacy globals classes: convert the TSX to Tailwind first, then
  delete the unused CSS in the same change. Do not leave orphaned selectors.
